       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/fh358rd2268.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "Crop 1 carries a stamp in printer's type, every figure plain: a vertical rule, then 1 8 2 2 5, then a block of three horizontal rules. Read as 18.2.25 on the convention that separators are dropped, which is the only valid date parse of the five figures. Low confidence because the doubt is not in the figures but in the kind of mark: set in type between rules, it could equally be a production or serial number rather than a punch date, so roll_number left null rather than claimed either way. Crop 3 has pencil at the very top edge of the scanned strip, '25' then a two-figure group, the upper half of every figure cut off by the edge in both panels, so it cannot be read and is not used here. Crops 2 and 4 hold only perforations and damp spots."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
